#: ../../tools/rxclass_tools.rst:109 192305cef39245748cd0c34540a84cbe
msgid ""
"**Description**: Get drug classification from NLM RxClass for a drug name"
" or RXCUI. Returns ATC codes, EPC (Established Pharmacologic Class), MoA,"
" VA drug classes, and more. No API key required. Example: 'metformin' -> "
"ATC A10BA02 (biguanides); 'aspirin' -> ATC N02BA01, EPC 'Platelet "
"Aggregation Inhibitor'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/rxclass_tools.rst:113 6ccb887a33f24511b82b3078065a931b
msgid ""
"``drug_name`` (string, null) (optional) Drug name to classify. Examples: "
"'metformin', 'aspirin', 'ibuprofen', 'metoprolol'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/rxclass_tools.rst:116 656cdc27e49e4dd7973d9a4af95fc344
msgid ""
"``rxcui`` (string, null) (optional) RxNorm RXCUI identifier (alternative "
"to drug\\_name). Examples: '6809' (metformin), '1191' (aspirin)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/rxclass_tools.rst:119 c7862ed363dc4216a707115b7aa5f9dc
msgid ""
"``rela_source`` (string, null) (optional) Classification source. Options:"
" 'ATC' (WHO Anatomical Therapeutic Chemical, default), 'FDASPL' (FDA "
"pharmacologic classes including EPC/MoA/PE), 'MESH', 'VA', 'DAILYMED', "
"'ALL'. Default: 'ATC'."
msgstr ""

